 ],
 "confidence": 0.9,
 "old_intent": "To illustrate the growing disparity in after-tax income growth between the wealthiest Americans and the middle and bottom classes over the last four decades.",
 "narration": "The wealthy are definitely under taxed. In the U .S., the disparity between the richest Americans and everyone else has been growing. And in the last 40 years, the after -tax income of the richest has risen more than 400 percent, while middle -class income has only risen 50. The way these people make money is very different than the way these people make money. And they're not taxed the same.",
